{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/771313-beasts-and-possession","id":771313,"title":"Beasts and Possession","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-22T01:14:04-08:00","id":771313,"title":"Beasts and Possession","content":"STs, what would you say happens when a Beast is possessed by entities capable of doing so? I'm especially curious about Strix, specifically.<br /> <br /> My initial instinct is that although they lose control of their body, their mind is free to focus on 'controlling' their Horror/Soul in the Primordial Dream, using it to feed or possibly arranging an exorcism of sorts. How would all of you run it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 11-22-2015, 04:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T01:40:07-08:00","id":771321,"title":"","content":"That sounds about right, at least if the strix doesn't use synthesis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T03:07:57-08:00","id":771352,"title":"","content":"I'm also curious about the possibility of a Beast being Claimed by a spirit, if it's even possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T04:20:12-08:00","id":771382,"title":"","content":"Personally, I argue that a possessing entity doesn't get command of mental abilitiies, but does get physical enhancements. In terms of Beast, that would be Atavisms and not Nightmares. No option to spend Satiety. <br /> <br /> When possessed, I believe the mind of the victim goes dormant, but you could make a case for either, depending on the plot you run.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T04:48:18-08:00","id":771394,"title":"","content":"I think claiming spirits kind of slot into the same space as their host's soul does, so they'd probably end up in the Beast's lair. From there you could either have it merge with the horror or stay a separate entity the Beast could communicate with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T11:08:04-08:00","id":771608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/771313-beasts-and-possession?p=771394#post771394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think claiming spirits kind of slot into the same space as their host's soul does, so they'd probably end up in the Beast's lair. From there you could either have it merge with the horror or stay a separate entity the Beast could communicate with.</div> </div> </div> </div>The narrative potential of some kind of powerful spirit possessing what looks like a normal person and then ending up the the Primordial Dream facing some ancient nightmare...I like this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T11:10:58-08:00","id":771610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/771313-beasts-and-possession?p=771394#post771394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think claiming spirits kind of slot into the same space as their host's soul does, so they'd probably end up in the Beast's lair. From there you could either have it merge with the horror or stay a separate entity the Beast could communicate with.</div> </div> </div> </div>*Spirit Tries to Claim a Beast, Beast Soul sits happily waiting* &quot;Ow.. this is the third one of these i've had the Chance to Snack on.... &quot; *Noms Down the Spirit*<br /> <br /> I'd imagine after the first time the Begotten would be able to Claim Kinship to a Spirit and maybe work on Nightmares that would Effect Spirits afterwards... But that would be up to the ST.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T14:56:18-08:00","id":771740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickmanUK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/771313-beasts-and-possession?p=771610#post771610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> *Spirit Tries to Claim a Beast, Beast Soul sits happily waiting* &quot;Ow.. this is the third one of these i've had the Chance to Snack on.... &quot; *Noms Down the Spirit*<br /> <br /> I'd imagine after the first time the Begotten would be able to Claim Kinship to a Spirit and maybe work on Nightmares that would Effect Spirits afterwards... But that would be up to the ST.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have tentative ideas for a Spirit Kinship Nightmare. One plays on the hierarchical deference spirits have with those of higher rank. Another could deal with themes of possession. Details are still scarce, however.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T16:06:47-08:00","id":771803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/771313-beasts-and-possession?p=771608#post771608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The narrative potential of some kind of powerful spirit possessing what looks like a normal person and then ending up the the Primordial Dream facing some ancient nightmare...I like this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. Don't go in the ocean if you're scared of sharks. If nothing else, Beasts should count as already Claimed, I'd think.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T16:51:51-08:00","id":771880,"title":"","content":"The relationship is way more awkward and tight than that. Even if you pick up a Horror instead of it merely incubating yours, your soul was in such a state that a Horror could slip in and count that as a metaphysically stable step up rather than an abysmal wreck of spiritual infrastructure. Sin Eaters are close to the Claimed than any Beast is.<br /> <br /> On a similar note though, there is still a division between human consciousness and spiritual existence, and a Beast's awareness and agency seems to do weird wandering circles between the two. This implies the flesh can still be ridden like a horse, even Claimed-you just have to contend with the dragon head that sits at the back end of the horse.<br /> <br /> So put me down with &quot;A Spirit can claim a Beast, but damn is it going to be uncomfortable&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T22:11:37-08:00","id":772082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/771313-beasts-and-possession?p=771608#post771608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The narrative potential of some kind of powerful spirit possessing what looks like a normal person and then ending up the the Primordial Dream facing some ancient nightmare...I like this.</div> </div> </div> </div> What narrative potential were you thinking of? I see three options.<br /> <br /> 1) The invading spirit is stronger than the horror, in which case the beast is dead, which isn't much fun for the player.<br /> <br /> 2) The invading spirit is weaker, in which case the spirit is dead, which seems like a serious dud narratively speaking.<br /> <br /> 3) The horror and the spirit can't interact with each in any way, because different types of ephemerals are intangible to each other, in which case the beast now has a squatter. Although the idea of a beast having to find a decent exorcist for their lair is amusing. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T22:41:24-08:00","id":772098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/771313-beasts-and-possession?p=772082#post772082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What narrative potential were you thinking of? I see three options.<br /> <br /> 1) The invading spirit is stronger than the horror, in which case the beast is dead, which isn't much fun for the player.<br /> <br /> 2) The invading spirit is weaker, in which case the spirit is dead, which seems like a serious dud narratively speaking.<br /> <br /> 3) The horror and the spirit can't interact with each in any way, because different types of ephemerals are intangible to each other, in which case the beast now has a squatter. Although the idea of a beast having to find a decent exorcist for their lair is amusing.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Moving away from the extremes of the first two, and barring the third, I can see it more like a home invasion, so to speak. With the Beast having the home field advantage due to the confrontation taking place in his Lair. And the spirit is fighting to evict his Soul from its rightful place. That could lead to one of two things if the spirit comes out on top: a Rampant (and possibly Claimed) Beast, or an Unfettered one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 11-23-2015, 01:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T23:06:00-08:00","id":772105,"title":"","content":"The answer is almost certainly, &quot;No, a Beast cannot be Claimed because it already is.&quot;<br /> If it isn't that, then it's, &quot;Why don't you and my Horror fight and whoever wins gets to keep the body.&quot;<br /> <br /> Attempting to do so will at best do nothing, and at worst put you inside the Beast's Lair as an uninvited guest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Hige sceal \u00fe\u0113 heardra, heorte \u00fe\u0113 c\u0113nre,<br /> m\u014dd sceal \u00fe\u0113 m\u0101re, \u00fe\u0113 \u016bre m\u00e6gen lytla\u00f0.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8950-vithrir","name":"Vithrir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8950_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T00:54:59-08:00","id":772151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/771313-beasts-and-possession?p=772082#post772082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What narrative potential were you thinking of? I see three options.<br /> <br /> 1) The invading spirit is stronger than the horror, in which case the beast is dead, which isn't much fun for the player.<br /> <br /> 2) The invading spirit is weaker, in which case the spirit is dead, which seems like a serious dud narratively speaking.<br /> <br /> 3) The horror and the spirit can't interact with each in any way, because different types of ephemerals are intangible to each other, in which case the beast now has a squatter. Although the idea of a beast having to find a decent exorcist for their lair is amusing.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't let it get resolved off-camera or like any kind of white-room combat. 'Stronger' isn't all that relevant.<br /> <br /> Allow the player to control the Horror. They'll have the potential to use the Lair creatively to drive off the intruder. Of course, spirits don't actually die normal deaths if they get beaten to a pulp, so I'd say a defeat simply drives the spirit from the lair, allowing the player to have experienced a creative way to fight of Possession while emphasizing the differences between Beasts and mortals...and leaving room for a recurring antagonist later.<br /> <br /> If the invading Spirit wins, that sucks, but so does getting shot in the head or being Ridden for the rest of the game without the chance to fight it off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T02:34:40-08:00","id":772171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/771313-beasts-and-possession?p=772082#post772082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 3) The horror and the spirit can't interact with each in any way, because different types of ephemerals are intangible to each other, in which case the beast now has a squatter. Although the idea of a beast having to find a decent exorcist for their lair is amusing.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>No twilight in the Astral. Spirits and Goetia can interact just fine there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T15:22:43-08:00","id":772558,"title":"","content":"Anyway, getting back a little closer to the original question about strix possession, what do you folks think an enshadowed beast altered through synthesis would be like?<br /> <br /> Not that such things would be too common, since I figure kinship would mean that beasts would quickly notice the possession.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/771313-beasts-and-possession?p=772171#post772171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No twilight in the Astral. Spirits and Goetia can interact just fine there.</div> </div> </div> </div>While that applies in twilight, nothing in the 2d edition rules books actually says that rule is limited to twilight, actually.<br /> <br /> &quot;Instead of bodies formed of flesh and bone, ephemeral beings are made up of spiritual matter called ephemera, which comes in several varieties. These substances are both invisible and intangible to anything not comprised of the same sort of ephemera \u2014 ghosts can see and touch one another, but are<br /> invisible to most living people and don\u2019t interact with solid objects or even other ephemeral beings that aren\u2019t ghosts,&quot; pg 215 GMC.<br /> <br /> A ghost in the hisil is still made of ephemera, would it not, etc? So logically the rule about different types of ephemera would seem to still apply.<br /> <br /> I admit that your interpretation might have been rules as intended, since that's how things worked in 1st edition, but it's not rules as written. <br /> <br /> Did anyone ask about that after GMC came out? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":391,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","user":"StSword","date":". 11-23-2015, 10:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T16:55:03-08:00","id":773513,"title":"","content":"Yeah, no, that wouldn't work. Stuff in ephemeral realms gets shifted to being the right sort of ephemera because the frequency they normally exist on <i>isn't there</i>. Humans get shunted onto spirit frequency for sure, but everything else has to as well or otherwise ghosts and goetia would perceive the shadow as nothing but a blank void, because <i>everything</i> there is spirit-ephemera.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T18:27:42-08:00","id":773561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/771313-beasts-and-possession?p=773513#post773513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, no, that wouldn't work. Stuff in ephemeral realms gets shifted to being the right sort of ephemera because the frequency they normally exist on <i>isn't there</i>. Humans get shunted onto spirit frequency for sure, but everything else has to as well or otherwise ghosts and goetia would perceive the shadow as nothing but a blank void, because <i>everything</i> there is spirit-ephemera.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which would be a good reason not to venture there, yes? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> (I kid - I think they are still going to &quot;alien&quot; ephemerals in other realms, right?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T20:00:59-08:00","id":773601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/771313-beasts-and-possession?p=773513#post773513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, no, that wouldn't work. Stuff in ephemeral realms gets shifted to being the right sort of ephemera because the frequency they normally exist on <i>isn't there</i>. Humans get shunted onto spirit frequency for sure, but everything else has to as well or otherwise ghosts and goetia would perceive the shadow as nothing but a blank void, because <i>everything</i> there is spirit-ephemera.</div> </div> </div> </div>The writers might not see that as a problem.<br /> <br /> Essence thief doesn't address the issue (if any ephemeral being is the right kind of ephemera by nature of being in a particular area, then any angel with spirit gate or spirit with death gate can manage to steal essence from spirits or ghosts for free).<br /> <br /> Death and Spirit Gateway don't address the issue of ephemerals in the wrong spirit realm.<br /> <br /> For that matter, every ephemeral can sense sources of appropriate essence from up to a mile away, to an ephemeral with essence thief, that includes every other ephemeral, so a spirit with that numen in the underworld would be able to sense pretty much every around it, ditto an ephemeral with appropriate influences. A Death spirit would be able to sense things just fine in the underworld, since death is the basis for everything there. <br /> <br /> A spirit in the underworld might have to use manifestations just as if they were in the material world if it wanted to affect anything, we don't know yet.<br /> <br /> The Realm Gateway numen could be assumed to do so, since there's that bit about the unfettered mutating to match their environments, but I believe that's the only such comment yet in second edition, even though ghosts mutating in the hisil for example was mentioned.<br /> <br /> Of course the talk about ghosts in the hisil mentioned they feed like spirits, which might mean in second edition terms they have essence thief.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":391,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","user":"StSword","date":". 11-24-2015, 11:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}